            0.452,
            0.886,
            0.551
          ],
          "content": "What are your observations regarding plants and animals found in various regions? Discuss your observations with your classmates."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.526,
            0.55,
            0.886,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": "You might observe from Table 2.6 that the plants and animals found in one kind of region are different from those found in another kind of region."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.252,
            0.686,
            0.672,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": "During a discussion in the classroom, Alex recalls that he observed cactus plants with thick and fleshy stems in the deserts of Rajasthan (Fig. 2.9). Maya shares that she saw deodar trees in the Himalayas of Himachal Pradesh (Fig. 2.10). These trees are conical in shape and have flexible and sloping branches."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.684,
            0.689,
            0.915,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.864,
            0.672,
            0.905
          ],
          "content": "Notice that these two types of plants found in different regions are different"
